The accompanying Node.js 13.1.0 compatibility patch modifies excerpts from
Node.js, V8, GYP, and Jinja2 source. Node.js source is distributed under MIT;
V8, GYP, and Jinja2 source is distributed under their respective BSD
3-clause licenses. The applicable license texts and copyright notices are
installed with this package in its license directory.

Node.js 13.1.0 source:
https://nodejs.org/download/release/v13.1.0/node-v13.1.0.tar.gz
SHA256: df640a2f151f788d02dc25c91d80fffe06b4c3c72fbdee07ab9abd7c6879d6cd

The inspector UTF-16 compatibility changes are adapted from V8 commit
182d9c05e78b1ddb1cb8242cd3628a7855a0336f and its FreeBSD ports backport:
https://chromium.googlesource.com/v8/v8/+/182d9c05e78b1ddb1cb8242cd3628a7855a0336f
https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-ports/commit/1617a29594f0a2f73ca741638e97e591a6618365
Additional changes adapt this release to Python 3.11, current libc++, and
MidnightBSD. The legacy uint16_t inspector constructor is retained.

